<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating the interaction between engineered NK cells and cancer cells. iPSCs and NK-92 cell lines differentiate into NK cells, which express IL-15. The NK cells use receptors like CAR, NKG2D, and CD16 to engage cancer cells, leading to cancer cell destruction via perforin, Granzyme B, and death receptor pathways \(FASL/TRAIL\). IL-15 supports NK cell proliferation.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
